WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.530 --> 00:00:04.130
Your sales team should know why
every meeting is on the calendar.

2
00:00:04.270 --> 00:00:06.190
Here’s how CallTeam gets there.

3
00:00:06.930 --> 00:00:12.010
First, we agree on your offer, your buyers,
and what makes a meeting worth taking.

4
00:00:13.130 --> 00:00:17.230
Then we build a focused list, or work the leads you already have.

5
00:00:17.450 --> 00:00:22.130
In this example, we’re calling controllers
at distributors with several locations.

6
00:00:22.170 --> 00:00:25.490
A single-location business falls outside the brief.

7
00:00:26.210 --> 00:00:28.870
Before dialing, we prepare the message.

8
00:00:29.030 --> 00:00:31.410
You approve how we represent your company.

9
00:00:31.630 --> 00:00:35.930
A real caller asks how invoice approvals work today, then listens.

10
00:00:36.590 --> 00:00:42.010
If the buyer asks us to call next week,
we record the reason and schedule that callback.

11
00:00:42.950 --> 00:00:48.710
If there’s a useful fit, we confirm the problem,
the right person, and a clear reason to meet.

12
00:00:49.790 --> 00:00:56.030
Your salesperson receives the buyer’s context,
call notes, open questions, and agreed next step.

13
00:00:57.290 --> 00:01:00.670
And you see what we’re learning through clear campaign updates.

14
00:01:01.850 --> 00:01:03.230
That’s CallTeam.

15
00:01:03.330 --> 00:01:07.930
Prospect research, human calling,
follow-up, and qualified appointments.

16
00:01:08.070 --> 00:01:10.050
See how we’d approach your market.

17
00:01:10.090 --> 00:01:14.499
Book a free strategy call at CallTeam.ca.
